WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.690
You won the Emmy this year. What was that-

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:06.210
What was that like? Tell me,
cause I've never won one.

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.400
You haven't? Well, you should have.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.080
It's just. I don't know.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.430
Surely you've been nominated.

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:14.333
I have been, I'm a perennial bridesmaid.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.470
Did you get sucked into the game

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:17.830
when you were nominated?

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:20.130
As Tom Hanks calls it, the trophy run.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:23.220
This is my favorite. He
said that with no irony.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.130
He said, "Yeah, I know it's, you know,

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:27.060
around the holidays, usually it's kind of

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.667
involved in the trophy run, so."

00:00:28.667 --> 00:00:30.262
And I thought, wow, that is the greatest.

00:00:30.262 --> 00:00:31.270
Ah that's great.

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:32.173
The trophy run.

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:34.830
And he has been many times.

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:37.574
And he has been. And
it's like Ty Cobb said,

00:00:37.574 --> 00:00:39.650
"It ain't bragging if you've done it."

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:43.680
And he'd done it many
times. What was it like?

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:46.040
How, did you think you were going to win?

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:49.900
No, I honestly didn't and I felt like

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.540
I was getting set up because, you know,

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:54.490
my agent kept sending me things, you know,

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:57.600
pieces that said I was going to win.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.820
And, and I thought, Nope, I've seen this.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.460
I won't name names, but
I've seen this happen

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:02.900
to too many people where they're

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:05.090
set up, you know? And I kept thinking it

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:07.200
for your consideration of the movie.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.763
So no by the time,

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:11.880
it was going to be announced.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.010
I had convinced myself,
no, I wasn't going to.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:15.860
And I wanted the show to win.

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:18.085
I thought that would be so
great for Eugene and Daniel.

00:01:18.085 --> 00:01:20.250
I really did want the show to win,

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.350
but I did not honest
to God didn't expect it

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:25.300
and was so happy to be with everyone.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:28.330
You know, we, I think Daniel talked Eugene

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:29.220
into having something. And so it was

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:32.290
going to be a barbecue
in Eugene's backyard.

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:33.860
Then there was the whole COVID thing.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.850
And then they had, I
think 50 people invited

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:39.790
two days before and they moved it

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:41.790
to where we were Castle Loma in Toronto.

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:45.350
It was kind of an event
place as old castle.

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:49.750
And then two days before the Emmys

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:54.750
or before the party, the
Ontario premier changed the law

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:59.120
so that it was maximum 25 people outdoors,

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:02.430
maximum 10 indoors. They had
to un invite or disinvite

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:03.750
half the people. And there were

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:06.220
all people who'd been
nominated for the show.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:09.280
And of course everybody we
wanted to see and be with.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:11.150
So that part was sad,
but then we got there

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:12.430
and then I looked at our world dressed

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:13.595
up and we got, I thought, how are we,

00:02:13.595 --> 00:02:16.620
how do we have stylists for a Zoom thing?

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:18.280
What are we doing?

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.210
Well you could wear. You could be naked

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:23.850
from the waist down. Nobody would know.

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:26.160
Well, apparently you do find out.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.100
That's right.

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:30.193
Oh dear. What was he thinking?

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.270
Yeah. So we got all dressed up.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:34.390
And when I got there, I thought, Oh

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:36.260
this looks like we think
we're going to win.

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:39.110
This is almost too pretty
and too fancy and too lovely.

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:41.260
And we had this lovely
dinner party and they had two

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.430
producers and a big screen
and you could see the other

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:47.550
nominees. And, and they said, okay.

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:49.150
And we all got tested of course.

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:51.430
We're safe to be with each other,

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:53.870
but we wore masks. And
they said, but if you win,

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:56.340
you're going to go up to
a microphone. Oh, come on.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:57.650
That looks like we think
we're going to win.

00:02:57.650 --> 00:02:59.370
Can we just stay in our seats if win?

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:01.097
And I'm not thinking
we're going to. He said,

00:03:01.097 --> 00:03:02.640
"Well everyone else is going
to go to the microphone."

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.850
Okay. So then I look
like I can't walk. Okay.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:07.020
So I have to go if I,
if I do, but I won't.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:10.260
Okay. And they say, okay,
we're about to start.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:13.023
And your category is the first one up.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.620
Just because it makes
you feel kind of sickly,

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:20.660
but then Jimmy Kimmel and
Jennifer Aniston did that

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:22.720
ridiculous bit with the fire,

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:25.010
burning out the card and not
for a second was I thinking,

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:27.640
Oh hurry. Get to it. I was just laughing.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:28.730
You know, at their silly bit.

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:30.980
She kept, she was so good
with the extinguisher.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:33.210
Just yeah. Better go at it again.

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:34.873
Yeah. This looks bad.

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:37.900
And then he read my name
and I have that card now,

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:40.640
Jimmy Kimmel sent it to me, so great.

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:43.800
Half burned away, but my
name is still in there.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.760
Yeah. And then, sorry,
I've gone on way too long,

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:50.550
but, and then Eugene won and
then Daniel won for writing.

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:53.280
And then it got to Annie
and she's sitting beside me.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:56.603
And I said, it was about
to announce her category.

00:03:56.603 --> 00:03:58.380
I said, "Now you have to win. Sorry."

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:00.237
"You actually have to win now."

00:04:00.237 --> 00:04:03.057
Now you have to. And she said to me,

00:04:03.057 --> 00:04:06.470
"Who do I apologize to first?"

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:07.493
It was insane.

